          "text": "chiming in here:\n\nwhen i visited China a while back, i asked one of my tour guides, a photographer, about what he thought “Marxism” and all that jazz\n\nhe gave me a quizzical look and was like “yeah i mean like we ‘d studied him in school and shit but nbd”\n\ni was like “oh, okay”\n\n& then we started talking about his new Fujifilm (or Canon, can’t remember) camera and he got a couple flicks of ya boy\n\ni realized that one of the hidden beauties of communism, as its practiced in China, is that the average person doesn’t have to think about the ideology because the ideology proves itself every single day\n\nthe trains run on time\n\nthe streets are clean\n\nfood was plentiful and cheap\n\nso for me, as some dumb westerner, to ask questions about communism to him is kinda silly because why would you question something that just works?\n\ni might as well asked, “well how does the sun rise and set everyday”\n\n“idk it just fucking does, now checkout this bad boy of a camera here”"
